times long after!) This lack of privacy leads to some very public displays of affection – what you see on the metro or trams won't…"],["Petřín Lookout Tower","sight",50.08354,14.39505,"","","","","","r","A smaller version of the Eiffel Tower on the top of Petrin Hill overlooking Prague. The grounds near the tower contain a formal rose garden which is free to walk around. With a height of just under 60 m, it is about 1/5th scale of the…"],["Strahov Monastery","sight",50.0862,14.3891,"","","","","","r","A monastery on the mountain. Worth a visit for both its picture gallery and its notable Renaissance library."],["National Gallery Prague - Old Masters","sight",50.09049,14.39722,"Hradčanské Square 2 and 15, Prague 1","Tue-Sun 10:00-18:00","","","","r","The Old Masters collection of the National Gallery, covering paintings from the 15th to 18th centuries, is divided between two mansions on Hradčanské Square, the Renaissance Schwarzenberg Palace and the Baroque Sternberg Palace."],["U Zavesenyho Kafe","restaurant",50.08844,14.39563,"Uvoz 6","","","","","r","one of the very few restaurants in the tourist area of Prague with a quirky atmosphere that isn't excessively touristy. Offering food at reasonable prices and serving good, modest food. A great place to have lunch while exploring…"],["LoVeg","restaurant",50.08853,14.39825,"Nerudova 36","11:30-22:00","","","","r","Vegan restaurant serving local Czech dishes and international cuisine."],["Museum of Public Transport","sight",50.09398,14.38939,"Patočkova 132/2, Praha 6","09:00-17:00, Sat, Sun and public holidays","","","","r","A storehouse of superbly restored trams from Hapsburg-era four-wheelers to the iconic Tatra cars of the Communist era. Also trolleybuses, buses and service vehicles. It can occasionally look closed during opening times - try the metal…"]]}